direction: down
title: "COMPLETION GUARD OWNS MORE THAN A DEPTH COUNTER\nProposed contract; no implementation or native test"
title.shape: text
entry: "Before callouts, register identities\nTarget + epoch; ExecEnv + root; activation + native call\nKeep Gambit root / marker and resource custody"
active: "Active / returning\nRecord old trace future writers and cleanup effects\nRelease service lock before synchronous callouts"
suspend: "Yielded / suspended\nRetain owned logical activation and live environment\nDo not retain a returned native stack pointer"
rewind: "Deletion / shutdown requests rewind\nSaved result + activated cleanup callbacks\nNo next-epoch publication yet"
terminal: "Terminal cleanup and caller restoration\nZero depth or empty one-environment root is insufficient\nNative calls, snapshots and resource effects must return"
local: "Local invocation complete\nDischarge local duties; transfer target custody upward\nNever wait on the blocked ancestor"
control: "Control owner settles admitted producers\nSourceReset event != OwnedReset != ReusableReceipt\nUnknown raw producer keeps reuse unresolved"
publish: "Publish next epoch only with full custody closure\nModern C and Zig require the same semantic support\n0 runtime paths retired; 0 exclusive Zig eliminations proved"
entry -> active
active -> suspend -> active
suspend -> rewind -> terminal
active -> terminal -> local -> control -> publish
suspend.style.fill: "#DFEEFF"
terminal.style.fill: "#FFF0E5"
publish.style.fill: "#E8F4E8"
